+# Cache Eviction Policy
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use an LRU (least recently used) eviction policy for the cache layer, with a fixed time-to-live (TTL) of 300 seconds applied to all cache entries. The rationale on record is operational simplicity: LRU with a fixed TTL gives predictable behavior that is easier to reason about and troubleshoot than frequency-based eviction.
